==============================================================================
GATE G2 — THE IoC KEYSTONE: what key period does flat IoC actually exclude?
==============================================================================
  Claim under test: 'perfectly flat IoC is only reachable by a FULL-LENGTH keystream'.
  Method: encipher real English-in-futhorc with a random periodic key of period k,
          measure ciphertext IoC.N at N=12956, 200 trials per k.
          Detection = IoC.N above the flat-null 95th percentile (>= mean+1.645sd).

  English-in-futhorc baseline: IoC.N = 1.8147  doublet = 2.856%
  flat null (uniform, N=12956): IoC.N mean 1.00000 sd 0.00056 -> 95th pct threshold 1.00093

   period k  mean IoC.N       sd  %trials detected
  --------------------------------------------------
          1     1.81471  0.00000            100.0%
          2     1.41958  0.14866            100.0%
          5     1.16251  0.05433            100.0%
         10     1.07838  0.03524            100.0%
         20     1.03703  0.01725            100.0%
         30     1.03018  0.01557            100.0%
         40     1.02199  0.01109            100.0%
         60     1.01303  0.00634            100.0%
         80     1.01091  0.00570            100.0%
        120     1.00648  0.00347            100.0%
        200     1.00381  0.00191             98.3%
        400     1.00215  0.00165             76.7%
       1000     1.00089  0.00082             45.0%
       3000     1.00025  0.00063             16.7%
      12956     0.99994  0.00059              6.7%

  p* (smallest period NOT reliably detected by IoC at N=12956) = 400
  Theory check: IoC.N(k) ~= 1 + (IoC.N_english - 1)/k = 1 + 0.8147/k
  G2 CONFIRMED — flat IoC bounds period from below at ~400, NOT at 12956

==============================================================================
GATE G3 — THE DOUBLET BOUND (a theorem, not a simulation)
==============================================================================
  For additive c = p + k (mod 29) with k statistically INDEPENDENT of p:
     P(c_i = c_{i-1}) = P(Dp + Dk = 0) = sum_d Pdp(d) * Pdk(-d)  >=  min_d Pdp(d)
  This class contains: every external one-time pad, every PRNG/hash keystream,
  every raw keytext, every TRANSFORMED keytext, every long derived key.
  If min_d Pdp(d) > 0.664%, the observed rate refutes the WHOLE class.

      corpus        n    IoC.N    dbl%   min_d Pdp(d) %  argmin d
  ----------------------------------------------------------------
         kjv   200000    1.734   2.912           1.5025         4
        moby   200000    1.692   3.565           1.8155         7
       pride   200000    1.718   3.409           1.7705        18
         war   200000    1.715   3.678           1.8095        18
   LP-solved      180    1.224   1.676           1.1173        17   (small n — reported, not relied on)

  Least favourable large corpus: min_d Pdp(d) = 1.5025%   vs OBSERVED 0.664%
  G3 CONFIRMED — observed doublet rate is BELOW the theoretical floor of the entire
     plaintext-independent-key class (external pads included).

  POSITIVE CONTROL for G3 (is the bound real and tight?):
    (a) English + TRUE RANDOM PAD          -> doublet 3.597%   (predicted 100/29 = 3.448%)
    (b) English + adversarial arithmetic key k_i = 25*i mod 29
        -> doublet 1.497%   (predicted min_d Pdp(d) = 1.503%)   IoC.N = 1.0001
        This is the BEST any independent key can do, and it is still 2.3x the observed rate.

